                <h2>Introduction: Why Independent Websites Need a Standardized Budget Allocation Process</h2>
<p>Many independent website teams fall into two extremes when starting ad campaigns: either burning money blindly on testing, or being too conservative with budget leading to insufficient data. Lack of a clear budget allocation SOP not only reduces testing efficiency but may also cause wasteful spending on ineffective campaigns.</p>
<p>This article outlines a complete standard process for budget allocation, suitable for teams with monthly budgets between $7,000 to $70,000 USD. It can be followed directly in operations.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Define Campaign Objectives and Stages</h2>
<p>Before allocating budget, you must confirm which stage you are in, as budget strategies differ significantly across stages.</p>
<p><strong>Stage Definition Criteria:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Stage</th>
<th>Core Objective</th>
<th>Typical Duration</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Cold Start (0-30 days)</td>
<td>Accumulate data, validate creatives and audiences</td>
<td>Testing-focused</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Growth Period (31-90 days)</td>
<td>Scale efficient channels, control CAC</td>
<td>Optimization &amp; scaling</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Stable Period (90+ days)</td>
<td>Maintain ROI, explore new channels</td>
<td>Stable operation</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Operational Key Points:</strong><br />
- During cold start, don't pursue ROI; focus on acquiring effective conversion data<br />
- In growth period, dynamically adjust budget based on CPA and LTV data<br />
- Record start and end dates for each stage for later review</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Evaluate Channel Characteristics and Cost Structure</h2>
<p>Different ad channels have varying speed of scaling, CPC/CPM levels, and conversion paths. Understand these before allocating.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Channel</th>
<th>Suitable Categories</th>
<th>Cold Start Difficulty</th>
<th>Recommended Initial Share</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta (Facebook/Instagram)</td>
<td>General categories, fashion &amp; home</td>
<td>Medium</td>
<td>40%-50%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads</td>
<td>Products with search demand</td>
<td>Low</td>
<td>20%-30%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>Young audience, high visual impact products</td>
<td>High</td>
<td>15%-25%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Other channels (Pinterest/Snapchat)</td>
<td>Specific verticals</td>
<td>High</td>
<td>5%-10%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Practical Recommendations:</strong><br />
- For first-time testing, prioritize Meta and Google due to mature backend tools and fast data feedback<br />
- TikTok suits teams with strong short video creative performance; new teams can test with small budgets<br />
- Minimum initial test budget per channel should be at least $70-140 USD daily</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Establish Initial Budget Allocation Ratios</h2>
<p>After channel evaluation, allocate monthly total budget using the following framework:</p>
<p><strong>Budget Allocation Formula:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Total Budget = Testing Budget (40%) + Main Campaign Budget (45%) + Contingency Reserve (15%)</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Testing Budget Allocation Logic:</strong><br />
- Further split testing budget into creative testing (60%) and audience testing (40%)<br />
- Minimum budget per test group should be 3-5x that channel's daily budget<br />
- Recommended to run no more than 10 creative/audience combinations simultaneously</p>
<p><strong>Main Campaign Budget Allocation Logic:</strong><br />
- Allocate to verified high-performing ad groups<br />
- Single ad group budget cap should not exceed 30% of daily total budget<br />
- Reserve 20% for scaling proven winning creatives</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Execute Budget Control During Testing Period</h2>
<p><strong>Daily Checklist:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Review previous day's spend and conversion data across all channels</li>
<li>[ ] Pause ad groups with high spend but zero conversions</li>
<li>[ ] Identify ad groups with CPA below target by 30%+; consider increasing budget</li>
<li>[ ] Record any anomalies (such as sudden CTR drops or abnormal CVR)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Testing Period Budget Adjustment Rules:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Situation</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Single ad group has no conversion within 7 days</td>
<td>Pause and release budget to other groups</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Single ad group CPA reaches 2x target</td>
<td>Observe for 2 days; pause if still exceeding</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Overall channel data exceeds expectations</td>
<td>Can increase from testing budget by 10%-20%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Overall channel data underperforms</td>
<td>Prioritize creative or audience optimization before deciding to pause</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Iterate and Optimize Budget Based on Data</h2>
<p>After the testing period (typically 2-3 weeks), reallocate budget based on data.</p>
<p><strong>Decision Matrix:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Channel Performance</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>High ROI + High Volume</td>
<td>Increase budget to 1.5-2x current</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High ROI + Low Volume</td>
<td>Expand audience or relax targeting</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Low ROI + High Volume</td>
<td>Optimize landing page, lower bids</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Low ROI + Low Volume</td>
<td>Pause; transfer budget to efficient channels</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Budget Reallocation Frequency:</strong><br />
- Conduct comprehensive review every two weeks<br />
- Monthly review should re-examine whether channel mix needs adjustment<br />
- Before major shopping events (Black Friday, Cyber Monday), concentrate resources on main channels 2 weeks in advance</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 6: Establish Budget Alert and Risk Control Mechanisms</h2>
<p><strong>Set Budget Alert Thresholds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Alert triggered when single channel daily spend exceeds 120% of set value</li>
<li>Alert when single ad group spend exceeds 50% of weekly budget with fewer than 5 conversions</li>
<li>Alert when total account balance falls below 3 days of projected spending</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Pre-spending Checklist to Prevent Waste:</strong><br />
- [ ] Confirm conversion tracking code (Pixel/SDK) is installed correctly<br />
- [ ] Check landing page load speed; eliminate invalid spend caused by technical issues<br />
- [ ] Verify audience overlap; avoid repeated exposure of same users across channels<br />
- [ ] Audit ad copy and landing page consistency; avoid high bounce rates</p>
